<BaseLayout title="About" description="About the independent Run PSL local running guide."><header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h1>About</h1><p>A simpler way to discover where, when, and with whom to run around Port St. Lucie.</p><span class="verified">Last verified July 15, 2026</span></div></header><article class="prose shell"><h2>An independent community project</h2><p>Run PSL gathers links to public running information in one mobile-friendly place. It is not an official City of Port St. Lucie website and does not represent the organizations it links to.</p><h2>Accuracy policy</h2><p>Freshness-sensitive listings display a verification date and link to a public source. Runners should confirm schedules, registration details, park conditions, and safety information directly with the responsible organization.</p><h2>Small by design</h2><p>The first version focuses on events, recurring group runs, routes, and useful local resources. It does not collect workout or health data.</p></article></BaseLayout>
